Runtime: cvt.w.s saturates a value of 2^31 and beyond to the largest 32-bit number (by sign).

What it fixes: FPU_CVT_W_S was `(int32_t)nearbyintf(a)`: for a positive value that does not fit, x86's conversion returns
0x80000000, where the reference emulator's interpreter (third_party/pcsx2/pcsx2/FPU.cpp, CVT_W) returns 0x7FFFFFFF for a
positive value whose exponent field is above 157 (2^31 and beyond, infinity and NaN patterns included) and 0x80000000 for a
negative one. The value inside the range is truncated (the cast truncates whatever the rounding mode is).

How it was verified: tests/conformance family "fpu", cvt.w.s: 14 of 61 cases differed before (2147483648.0, 3.4e38 and the
exponent-all-ones patterns, positive) and none after. 911 cvt.w.s sites in the game; a position or a timer that grows past 2^31
before the conversion is the plausible way to meet it. Applies to the macro, so no regeneration of the generated code is
needed, only a rebuild.

Original work for this repository (no code from another project).

diff --git a/ps2xRuntime/include/ps2_runtime_macros.h b/ps2xRuntime/include/ps2_runtime_macros.h
--- a/ps2xRuntime/include/ps2_runtime_macros.h
+++ b/ps2xRuntime/include/ps2_runtime_macros.h
@@ -623,7 +623,17 @@
 #define FPU_FLOOR_W_S(a) ((int32_t)floorf((float)(a)))
 #define FPU_CVT_S_W(a) ((float)(int32_t)(a))
 #define FPU_CVT_S_L(a) ((float)(int64_t)(a))
-#define FPU_CVT_W_S(a) ((int32_t)nearbyintf((float)(a)))
+// cvt.w.s: truncation; a value whose exponent is above 157 (2^31 and beyond, infinities and NaN patterns included) saturates
+// by sign (FPU.cpp: CVT_W). The plain C cast gives 0x80000000 for the positive ones.
+static inline int32_t ps2_fpu_cvt_w_s(float f)
+{
+    uint32_t u;
+    std::memcpy(&u, &f, sizeof(u));
+    if ((u & 0x7F800000u) <= 0x4E800000u)
+        return (int32_t)f;
+    return (u & 0x80000000u) ? INT32_MIN : INT32_MAX;
+}
+#define FPU_CVT_W_S(a) ps2_fpu_cvt_w_s((float)(a))
 #define FPU_CVT_L_S(a) ((int64_t)(float)(a))
 #define FPU_C_F_S(a, b) (0)
 #define FPU_C_UN_S(a, b) (isnan((float)(a)) || isnan((float)(b)))
